 ## Overview
-Image-aligned splatting is a volume rendering technique that eliminates color bleeding and popping artifacts by aligning the compositing sheet with the image plane at all times, regardless of the viewing direction [S2, S3, unofficial]. Unlike its sibling [Axis-Aligned Sheet-Buffered Splatting](5593-axis-aligned-sheet-buffered-splatting.md), which organizes voxels into fixed volume slices parallel to the viewing axis, image-aligned splatting advances a slab across the volume, slicing and projecting all intersecting kernels into sheet buffers [S2, unofficial]. This approach provides the most accurate reconstruction of the voxel field prior to compositing and produces smoother images with better anti-aliasing characteristics than raycasting, though at a higher computational cost due to multiple splatting of voxels [S2, unofficial][S4].
+Image-aligned splatting is a volume rendering technique that eliminates color bleeding and popping artifacts by aligning the compositing sheet with the image plane at all times, regardless of the viewing direction [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. Unlike its sibling [Axis-Aligned Sheet-Buffered Splatting](5593-axis-aligned-sheet-buffered-splatting.md), which organizes voxels into fixed volume slices parallel to the viewing axis, image-aligned splatting advances a slab across the volume, slicing and projecting all intersecting kernels into sheet buffers [S2, unofficial][S4, book]. This approach provides the most accurate reconstruction of the voxel field prior to compositing and produces smoother images with better anti-aliasing characteristics than raycasting, though at a higher computational cost due to multiple splatting of voxels [S2, unofficial][S4, book].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** Volume dataset (density, color, opacity fields), viewing parameters (viewpoint, direction, projection matrix), slab width $\Delta s$, kernel base distribution.
-**Outputs:** Final composited image.
+**Inputs:** Volume dataset containing density, color, and opacity fields [S2, unofficial][S4, book]. Viewing parameters including viewpoint, direction, and projection matrix [S3, unofficial]. Slab width $\Delta s$ [S3, unofficial]. Kernel base distribution and scaling factor [S1, unofficial].
+**Outputs:** Final composited image buffer.
 
 **Data Structures:**
-1.  **Sheet Buffer:** A 2D buffer aligned with the image plane, storing accumulated color $C$ and opacity $\alpha$ for the current slab.
-2.  **Occlusion Map:** A dynamically computed screen-space map used for early splat elimination, updated via convolution after each sheet composite.
-3.  **Kernel Sections:** Pre-integrated footprints of voxel kernels, stacked to form a single kernel representation.
